# Test Directory

This project mostly uses dedicated PlatformIO environments instead of the
default PlatformIO unit-test runner.

## Useful Test/Bench Environments

| Env | Command | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `test` | `pio run -e test` | On-target test harness from `src/test_main.cpp` |
| `fcu_bench_test` | `pio run -e fcu_bench_test -t upload` | Auto-sequenced ESC, motor direction, IMU, and mixer bench run |
| `fcu_motor_fft_test` | `pio run -e fcu_motor_fft_test -t upload` | Motor vibration logging firmware for FFT tools |
| `fcu_motor_fft_test_full_dshot` | `pio run -e fcu_motor_fft_test_full_dshot -t upload` | Full-range sweep variant for restrained test stands |
| `ekf_sim` | `pio run -e ekf_sim` | On-target EKF synthetic trajectory test |
| `native_ekf_sim` | `pio run -e native_ekf_sim` | Desktop/native EKF synthetic trajectory test |

## Safety

- Remove props for all motor direction and single-motor tests.
- Full-range or all-motor tests require a restrained airframe.
- Do not run PID webserver or bench-relaxed failsafe builds for flight.

## Commit Smoke Test

Before staging a large firmware change, a practical minimum is:

```pwsh
pio run -e esp32-s3-mini
pio run -e fcu_motor_fft_test
pio run -e fcu_bench_test
pio run -e native_ekf_sim
```
